# Definition of Done

The checklists every slice and every phase must satisfy before it is reported as done.

## Per slice

- [ ] Acceptance criteria (from `[roadmap/plan doc path]`) are met.
- [ ] Tests were written **first** (failing), then the minimum code to pass.
- [ ] Full test suite is green — no failing or skipped tests.
- [ ] Validator's tests are its **own** — written from the acceptance criteria, not read or
      borrowed from the implementer's test file.
- [ ] [Static-correctness gate command] clean.
- [ ] [Style/lint gate command(s)] clean.
- [ ] Coverage meets the agreed threshold ([coverage command]) — or the project's explicit,
      recorded decision not to use a coverage number applies.
- [ ] [If this project has a designer function: design/accessibility check done for any
      user-facing change. Delete this line if not applicable.]
- [ ] Performance/cost implications considered where this slice touches a budgeted concern (see
      `[team-brief path]`'s performance/cost section) — or not applicable, explicitly.
- [ ] Permanent project and process knowledge updated for the slice.
- [ ] ADR written if a decision was made, or an existing one superseded with its project-wide
      impact recorded.
- [ ] Durable knowledge promoted out of scratch; slice scratch cleaned.
- [ ] Commit follows this project's commit conventions, on a feature branch (or a parallel-work
      branch merged per this project's parallel-work policy).
- [ ] No forbidden action taken (see this project's boundaries doc — no production access, no
      secrets, no scope creep).
- [ ] Stakeholder sign-off received at whatever cadence was set during setup.

## Per phase / overall

- [ ] All slices done and reviewed.
- [ ] End-to-end behaviors match the spec via the local dev/run loop.
- [ ] Quickstart instructions work from a clean checkout.
- [ ] [Operator/manual verification checklist exists, if this project has infra seams that
      can't be automated.]
- [ ] Operational readiness (observability, rollback) reflects whatever this project decided
      during setup — see `[team-brief path]`'s operational-readiness section.
- [ ] Open-questions log is empty or explicitly deferred with rationale.
